From: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: let the TCL segment TCP batches

A TCP batch from mac80211 was split with skb_gso_segment(), which
allocates, maps and frees a buffer for every frame of it. The TCL can
segment a batch itself: a data command may point at an MSDU extension
descriptor that lists the batch's headers and one segment's payload, and
the TCL writes that segment's IP length, IP ID, TCP sequence number and
flags into the headers and fills in the checksums. Queue every segment
of a TSO batch that way, with one mapping of the headers and of each
payload piece, and complete the batch when its last segment completes.
Batches the TCL cannot take whole still go through skb_gso_segment().
The tso module parameter turns it off.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
---
